 A. Locke has a reputation of being one of the leading scholars in research and teaching about celiac diseases.   Dr. Locke graduated with a bachelor's degree of science.  He graduated Magna Cum Laude as a Master in Education from Teachers College/Columbia University, where he served on the Dean’s Council.
Dr. Locke works closely with several groups to combat the prevalence of celiac diseases, including the American College of Nutrition, the National Institutes of Health (NIH), University of California at Berkley, the Department of Health and Human in Health Care (USD HHS), Division of Nutrition Research Coordination (NRC), Institute of Medicine (IOM), Pediatric Nutrition Task Force (PNTF), Joint Action Plan (JANET) of International Association of Paediatricians (GPA) and Italian Pediatric Association.
He also serves with many government bodies at several levels. He is a member of the NIH’s Advisory Committee to the Director; a Special Fellow of the U.S. Department of Education;

